-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the reference meaning
-- the same calculus read without the machine (part of machine-in-hyperactive): a value is a head
-- with its parts, the parts values and not wires; an environment and a list of parts are lists of
-- values. There are no wires, no memory, no order of steps: a body's value is computed by
-- recursion. What an eliminator does with a value is asked of the same table, nk-act, and done
-- here by nk-ev-fire as nk-fire does it on wires: one table, two readers
data NkEv = nkev (h : NkHd) (ps : NkEv) | nkev-nil | nkev-cons (v : NkEv) (r : NkEv)
